{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nCTX='/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/quantum-physics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--quantum-physics/context.json'\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- scope ---'\njq '{metadata, scope, overview_id, source_record_count:(.source_records|length), claim_count:(.claims|length), relation_count:(.relations|length), topic_count:(.topics|length)}' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- source records from context ---'\njq -r '.source_records[]? | [.source_id, (.title // .display_title // .short_title // \\\"\\\"), (.authors // .author // \\\"\\\"), (.year // .published_year // \\\"\\\"), (.summary // .abstract // \\\"\\\")] | @json' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- claims compact ---'\njq -r '.claims[] | {claim_id, source_id, short_title, text} | @json' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- topics compact ---'\njq -r '.topics[]? | @json' \\\"\"'$CTX\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- relations compact ---'\njq -r '.relations[]? | @json' \\\"\"'$CTX\"'","aggregated_output":"--- scope ---\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"overview_id\": \"subspace--quantum-physics\",\n    \"parent_space_name\": \"physics\",\n    \"scope_kind\": \"subspace\",\n    \"scope_name\": \"quantum-physics\",\n    \"scope_title\": \"Quantum Physics\",\n    \"space_name\": \"quantum-physics\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": null,\n  \"overview_id\": null,\n  \"source_record_count\": 5,\n  \"claim_count\": 49,\n  \"relation_count\": 30,\n  \"topic_count\": 15\n}\n--- source records from context ---\n[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond\",[\"John Preskill\"],\"\",\"John Preskill frames the NISQ era as a real scientific threshold but warns against overclaiming near-term commercial transformation. Devices around 50 to a few hundred noisy qubits may illuminate many-body quantum physics and test heuristic algorithms, yet gate errors, circuit-depth limits, and error-correction overhead keep transformative fault-tolerant applications at a longer horizon.\"]\n[\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor\",[\"Frank Arute\",\"Kunal Arya\",\"Ryan Babbush\",\"Dave Bacon\",\"Joseph C. Bardin\",\"Rami Barends\",\"Rupak Biswas\",\"Sergio Boixo\",\"Fernando G. S. L. Brandao\",\"David A. Buell\",\"Brian Burkett\",\"Yu Chen\",\"Zijun Chen\",\"Ben Chiaro\",\"Roberto Collins\",\"William Courtney\",\"Andrew Dunsworth\",\"Edward Farhi\",\"Brooks Foxen\",\"Austin Fowler\",\"Craig Gidney\",\"Marissa Giustina\",\"Rob Graff\",\"Keith Guerin\",\"Steve Habegger\",\"Matthew P. Harrigan\",\"Michael J. Hartmann\",\"Alan Ho\",\"Markus Hoffmann\",\"Trent Huang\",\"Travis S. Humble\",\"Sergei V. Isakov\",\"Evan Jeffrey\",\"Zhang Jiang\",\"Dvir Kafri\",\"Kostyantyn Kechedzhi\",\"Julian Kelly\",\"Paul V. Klimov\",\"Sergey Knysh\",\"Alexander Korotkov\",\"Fedor Kostritsa\",\"David Landhuis\",\"Mike Lindmark\",\"Erik Lucero\",\"Dmitry Lyakh\",\"Salvatore Mandrà\",\"Jarrod R. McClean\",\"Matthew McEwen\",\"Anthony Megrant\",\"Xiao Mi\",\"Kristel Michielsen\",\"Masoud Mohseni\",\"Josh Mutus\",\"Ofer Naaman\",\"Matthew Neeley\",\"Charles Neill\",\"Murphy Yuezhen Niu\",\"Eric Ostby\",\"Andre Petukhov\",\"John C. Platt\",\"Chris Quintana\",\"Eleanor G. Rieffel\",\"Pedram Roushan\",\"Nicholas C. Rubin\",\"Daniel Sank\",\"Kevin J. Satzinger\",\"Vadim Smelyanskiy\",\"Kevin J. Sung\",\"Matthew D. Trevithick\",\"Amit Vainsencher\",\"Benjamin Villalonga\",\"Theodore White\",\"Z. Jamie Yao\",\"Ping Yeh\",\"Adam Zalcman\",\"Hartmut Neven\",\"John M. Martinis\"],\"\",\"The source reports Google's Sycamore experiment demonstrating task-specific quantum supremacy in random circuit sampling. It combines a 53-qubit programmable superconducting processor, cross-entropy benchmarking, component error modeling, and classical simulation cost estimates to argue that Sycamore performed a sampling task in minutes that would take state-of-the-art classical resources thousands of years at equal fidelity.\"]\n[\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"03-the-quantum-internet\",[\"H. J. Kimble\"],\"\",\"H. J. Kimble's The Quantum Internet frames quantum networks as systems of nodes and channels that require reversible light-matter interfaces, strong single-photon nonlinearities, ensemble memories, repeaters, and scalable verification. The source surveys cavity-QED and atomic-ensemble routes, emphasizing both experimental progress and the difficulty of extending and certifying entanglement in larger heterogeneous networks.\"]\n[\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor\",[\"Alberto Peruzzo\",\"Jarrod McClean\",\"Peter Shadbolt\",\"Man-Hong Yung\",\"Xiao-Qi Zhou\",\"Peter J. Love\",\"Alán Aspuru-Guzik\",\"Jeremy L. O’Brien\"],\"\",\"The source introduces and experimentally demonstrates a hybrid quantum-classical variational eigenvalue solver on an integrated photonic processor. Its central result is a proof-of-principle He-H+ molecular-energy calculation that trades QPE-style long coherent evolution for repeated short expectation-value measurements and classical optimization.\"]\n[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"05-quantum-machine-learning\",[\"Jacob Biamonte\",\"Peter Wittek\",\"Nicola Pancotti\",\"Patrick Rebentrost\",\"Nathan Wiebe\",\"Seth Lloyd\"],\"\",\"The source reviews quantum machine learning as a field built on possible quantum speedups for linear algebra, optimization, sampling, deep learning, and quantum-data analysis, while emphasizing that input, output, circuit-cost, and benchmarking constraints determine whether these speedups become practical.\"]\n--- claims compact ---\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Verification supports extrapolation\",\"text\":\"Agreement among full, patch, elided, and predicted fidelities on classically verifiable circuits supports using elided circuits to estimate fidelity in the supremacy regime.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-atomic-ensemble-experiments-had-achieved-stored-heralded-entanglement-high-retri--7d38956d9ede\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Ensemble experiments store entanglement\",\"text\":\"Atomic-ensemble experiments had achieved stored heralded entanglement, high retrieval efficiencies, and minimal scalable-node functionality by the time of the source discussion.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-circuit-depth-and-implementation-overhead-can-become-prohibitive-for-nominally-e--07b698d82789\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Overheads threaten practical speedups\",\"text\":\"Circuit depth and implementation overhead can become prohibitive for nominally exponential quantum machine learning speedups without substantial algorithmic optimization and realistic cost estimates.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-controlled-cavity-pulses-can-generate-entanglement-first-between-an-atom-and-an--ee045e1c7175\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Cavity pulses entangle photons\",\"text\":\"Controlled cavity pulses can generate entanglement first between an atom and an emitted photon and then between sequentially emitted photon polarizations.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Gate errors cap circuits\",\"text\":\"Current two-qubit gate and measurement error rates imply that uncorrected NISQ circuits cannot grow much beyond about one thousand fundamental two-qubit operations before noise overwhelms the signal.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Dark states map photons reversibly\",\"text\":\"Dark-state adiabatic control can reversibly map a single-photon optical field into a trapped atom and later map the stored atomic state back into a flying optical field.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-deep-quantum-learning-can-use-quantum-annealers-programmable-photonic-circuits-a--0bdb973219c3\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Special hardware supports deep learning\",\"text\":\"Deep quantum learning can use quantum annealers, programmable photonic circuits, and quantum Boltzmann machines rather than requiring a large universal quantum computer.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-device-ansatz-strategies-can-provide-variationally-optimal-solutions-for-the-ava--64cad93bb7ab\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"Device ansatz optimizes resources\",\"text\":\"Device ansatz strategies can provide variationally optimal solutions for the available quantum resources even when the ansatz differs from traditional chemistry-motivated forms.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"EIT maps photonic memories\",\"text\":\"Electromagnetically induced transparency enables deterministic reversible mapping of photonic states and photonic entanglement into and out of atomic-ensemble quantum memories.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-experimental-energy-estimates-are-limited-by-photon-source-impurity-photon-disti--780254eb8ba5\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"Noise shifts measured energies\",\"text\":\"Experimental energy estimates are limited by photon-source impurity, photon distinguishability, circuit imperfections, coupling imbalance, and increasing degeneracy-related difficulty at larger bond separations.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-for-the-demonstrated-4x4-hamiltonian-the-quantum-expectation-estimation-approach--8aea71f20a05\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"QEE reduces CNOT requirements\",\"text\":\"For the demonstrated 4x4 Hamiltonian, the quantum expectation-estimation approach uses fewer entangling-gate resources than phase estimation, requiring one CNOT gate instead of at least twelve.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum sampling outpaces classical\",\"text\":\"For the hardest reported random-circuit sampling task, Sycamore produced one million samples in about 200 seconds while the authors estimated equal-fidelity classical sampling would take about 10,000 years on one million cores.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-full-density-matrix-characterization-becomes-an-impractical-verification-strateg--65a0be3566e1\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Verification scales poorly\",\"text\":\"Full density-matrix characterization becomes an impractical verification strategy as quantum networks grow because the state description scales exponentially with network size.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"Hamiltonians decompose into Pauli expectations\",\"text\":\"Hamiltonian expectation values for a broad class of physical systems reduce to sums of Pauli-product expectation values measured on a quantum state.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum dynamics is promising\",\"text\":\"Highly entangled quantum dynamics is the most natural arena for meaningful quantum advantage, and noisy devices around one hundred qubits may already yield valuable physical insight.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"NISQ speedups remain uncertain\",\"text\":\"Hybrid QAOA and VQE approaches are plausible NISQ-era testbeds, but their ability to outperform mature classical approximation methods remains unresolved.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Networks require quantum interconnects\",\"text\":\"Large quantum networks require reversible interconnects that convert quantum states between matter and light while preserving coherence and entanglement.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-large-scale-quantum-random-access-memory-and-quantum-state-readout-constraints-c--fa6ae1d801a4\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Input output bottlenecks dominate\",\"text\":\"Large-scale quantum random access memory and quantum-state readout constraints can erase practical advantages for many linear-algebra-based quantum machine learning algorithms on classical data.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-linear-cross-entropy-benchmarking-provides-a-fidelity-measure-by-comparing-exper--4abac38b173d\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"XEB measures circuit fidelity\",\"text\":\"Linear cross-entropy benchmarking provides a fidelity measure by comparing experimentally observed bitstrings with ideal probabilities computed by classical simulation.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-lower-gate-error-rates-matter-both-because-they-allow-larger-uncorrected-nisq-ci--043e58605f51\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Better gates enable scale\",\"text\":\"Lower gate error rates matter both because they allow larger uncorrected NISQ circuits and because they reduce the future overhead of fault-tolerant error correction.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-measured-component-error-rates-under-simultaneous-operation-were-low-enough-to-s--6d6ae35745de\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Gate errors predict fidelity\",\"text\":\"Measured component error rates under simultaneous operation were low enough to support a model predicting measurable fidelity for full random circuits.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-nelder-mead-direct-search-was-more-robust-than-gradient-descent-for-the-noisy-ph--c886fbe39dc2\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"Nelder Mead handles photon noise\",\"text\":\"Nelder-Mead direct search was more robust than gradient descent for the noisy photonic optimization landscape and converged to the global minimum in most runs.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-nisq-computers-with-roughly-50-to-a-few-hundred-qubits-mark-a-classically-hard-s--2d5ec194bedf\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Noise limits NISQ depth\",\"text\":\"NISQ computers with roughly 50 to a few hundred qubits mark a classically hard simulation regime, but noisy gates place serious near-term limits on what they can compute.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"NISQ enables quantum exploration\",\"text\":\"NISQ devices are best understood as experimental tools for exploring many-body quantum physics and as stepping stones toward more powerful quantum technologies, not as near-term world-changing machines.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-noise-resilient-circuit-design-can-extend-nisq-computational-reach-but-it-may-tr--aed4bcfeaa39\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Noise resilience has tradeoffs\",\"text\":\"Noise-resilient circuit design can extend NISQ computational reach, but it may trade off against classical simulability.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"qBLAS enables exponential speedups\",\"text\":\"Quantum basic linear algebra subroutines provide exponential speedups for Fourier transforms, eigenvalue estimation, eigenvector finding, and linear equation solving relative to the best known classical counterparts.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-boltzmann-machine-training-can-gain-quadratic-improvements-in-thermaliza--2d6a13e72831\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum Boltzmann training accelerates\",\"text\":\"Quantum Boltzmann machine training can gain quadratic improvements in thermalization, sampling, and training-data access under quantum-coherent or qRAM access assumptions.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"NP-hard problems remain hard\",\"text\":\"Quantum computers are not expected to efficiently solve hard NP-hard combinatorial optimization instances, although they may provide modest search speedups or useful heuristic approximations.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum advantage has grounds\",\"text\":\"Quantum computers have credible grounds for super-classical power because of known quantum algorithms, complexity-theoretic sampling arguments, and the absence of efficient classical simulations of general quantum computation.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-connectivity-gives-linked-nodes-a-state-space-that-scales-exponentially--50cc8b700a70\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum channels expand state space\",\"text\":\"Quantum connectivity gives linked nodes a state space that scales exponentially across all nodes, unlike classically connected quantum processors whose state spaces remain separate by node.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-expectation-estimation-reduces-coherent-evolution-demands-relative-to-ph--e17864953251\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"QEE reduces coherent evolution\",\"text\":\"Quantum expectation estimation reduces coherent-evolution demands relative to phase estimation by replacing one long coherent evolution with many short expectation-value measurements.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum learning can accelerate analysis\",\"text\":\"Quantum machine learning can outperform classical algorithms on specific pattern-recognition and data-analysis tasks when quantum algorithms exploit coherence, entanglement, or quantum access models.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-for-quantum-data-can-reduce-tomography-and-characteriza--b02ec76133c0\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Quantum data avoids full tomography\",\"text\":\"Quantum machine learning for quantum data can reduce tomography and characterization costs by extracting principal components, dynamics, or expectation-value summaries without full state reconstruction.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-principal-component-analysis-can-diagonalize-a-covariance-like-density-m--6ee32a171ac2\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"qPCA diagonalizes quantum covariance\",\"text\":\"Quantum principal component analysis can diagonalize a covariance-like density matrix and estimate principal components exponentially more efficiently than classical PCA when data are available in quantum form.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Random circuits scale exponentially\",\"text\":\"Random quantum circuits become exponentially harder to simulate classically as qubit count and circuit depth increase because their output distributions lack exploitable structure.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\",\"source_id\":\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"short_title\":\"Error correction remains distant\",\"text\":\"Scalable fault-tolerant quantum computing depends on quantum error correction, but the physical-qubit overhead makes that era a longer-term objective rather than a near-term NISQ capability.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Heterogeneous networks need verification\",\"text\":\"Scalable quantum networks are likely to be heterogeneous systems that combine cavity-QED nodes, ensemble memories, repeaters, local processing, error-corrected teleportation, and stronger entanglement-verification procedures.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-strong-cavity-qed-coupling-supplies-a-physical-regime-in-which-individual-atoms--9807d4e35625\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"Strong coupling enables interfaces\",\"text\":\"Strong cavity-QED coupling supplies a physical regime in which individual atoms and photons can interact coherently enough to function as quantum-network nodes and interfaces.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-demonstrated-integrated-photonic-processor-prepares-and-measures-arbitrary-t--f41a0c8f645b\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"Photonic chip prepares two qubits\",\"text\":\"The demonstrated integrated photonic processor prepares and measures arbitrary two-qubit pure states using voltage-controlled phase shifters, one CNOT gate, photon-pair inputs, and detector count rates.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Fault tolerance remains necessary\",\"text\":\"The demonstrated speedup is specific to random circuit sampling and does not remove the need for fault-tolerant logical qubits for applications such as Shor-style factoring.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-dlcz-protocol-creates-heralded-entanglement-between-atomic-ensembles-by-inte--aa516185d3b2\",\"source_id\":\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"short_title\":\"DLCZ heralds ensemble entanglement\",\"text\":\"The DLCZ protocol creates heralded entanglement between atomic ensembles by interfering emitted single-photon fields and conditioning on a detector event.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"HHL has conditional advantage\",\"text\":\"The HHL linear-system algorithm can output a quantum state proportional to a solution vector in polylogarithmic time under sparsity, conditioning, input-preparation, and readout assumptions.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Elided circuits retain fidelity\",\"text\":\"The largest elided 53-qubit, 20-cycle circuits yielded F_XEB = (2.24 ± 0.21) × 10^-3 over 30 million samples, supporting an average fidelity above 0.1% with 5σ confidence.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-largest-random-circuits-combined-53-qubits-1-113-single-qubit-gates-430-two--c8ece98aae87\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Large circuits remain measurable\",\"text\":\"The largest random circuits combined 53 qubits, 1,113 single-qubit gates, 430 two-qubit gates, and one measurement per qubit, for which the authors predicted a total fidelity of 0.2%.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-near-term-viability-of-quantum-machine-learning-depends-on-solving-input-out--0091df09ad90\",\"source_id\":\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"short_title\":\"Viability needs practical benchmarks\",\"text\":\"The near-term viability of quantum machine learning depends on solving input, output, costing, and benchmarking problems rather than only proving asymptotic speedups.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-photonic-variational-eigensolver-experimentally-recovered-the-he-h-bond-diss--5898494f9b1f\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"QVE resolves He-H+ energy\",\"text\":\"The photonic variational eigensolver experimentally recovered the He-H+ bond-dissociation curve, finding an equilibrium bond length of 92.3±0.1 pm and a ground-state electronic energy of -2.865±0.008 MJ mol^-1 after correction.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-quantum-variational-eigensolver-prepares-approximate-ground-states-by-using--0037de1d8464\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"QVE minimizes Rayleigh Ritz energy\",\"text\":\"The quantum variational eigensolver prepares approximate ground states by using quantum expectation estimation inside a classical minimization of the Rayleigh-Ritz quotient.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-the-sycamore-superconducting-processor-created-random-circuit-quantum-states-on--2b4eeabd4063\",\"source_id\":\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"short_title\":\"Sycamore reaches 53 qubits\",\"text\":\"The Sycamore superconducting processor created random-circuit quantum states on 53 qubits, corresponding to a computational state space of 2^53, about 10^16 basis states.\"}\n{\"claim_id\":\"claim-unitary-coupled-cluster-ansatz-states-can-be-represented-with-polynomially-many--7f92a3b77387\",\"source_id\":\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"short_title\":\"UCC states favor quantum preparation\",\"text\":\"Unitary coupled-cluster ansatz states can be represented with polynomially many reduced cluster terms and are efficiently preparable on quantum hardware despite lacking a known efficient classical implementation.\"}\n--- topics compact ---\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-lower-gate-error-rates-matter-both-because-they-allow-larger-uncorrected-nisq-ci--043e58605f51\",\"claim-linear-cross-entropy-benchmarking-provides-a-fidelity-measure-by-comparing-exper--4abac38b173d\",\"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\",\"claim-measured-component-error-rates-under-simultaneous-operation-were-low-enough-to-s--6d6ae35745de\",\"claim-the-largest-random-circuits-combined-53-qubits-1-113-single-qubit-gates-430-two--c8ece98aae87\",\"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Preskill's NISQ framing emphasizes that two-qubit gate and measurement errors limit how large uncorrected quantum circuits can grow before noise overwhelms the signal. The Sycamore paper turns that limitation into a measurement problem by estimating fidelity for random circuits whose ideal outputs become difficult to compute directly.\",\"heading\":\"Noise as the benchmark target\"},{\"body\":\"Linear cross-entropy benchmarking compares experimentally observed bitstrings with ideal probabilities computed by classical simulation. Sycamore's component error rates under simultaneous operation supported a model that predicted measurable fidelity for full random circuits, including the largest circuits with 53 qubits, 1,113 single-qubit gates, 430 two-qubit gates, and one measurement per qubit.\",\"heading\":\"Cross-entropy and error models\"},{\"body\":\"The largest elided 53-qubit, 20-cycle circuits yielded F_XEB = (2.24 ± 0.21) × 10^-3 over 30 million samples, supporting average fidelity above 0.1% with 5σ confidence. Agreement among full, patch, elided, and predicted fidelities on classically verifiable circuits supports using elided circuits to estimate fidelity when direct full-circuit verification becomes infeasible.\",\"heading\":\"Evidence across verifiable regimes\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Benchmarking Noisy Quantum Computation\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-benchmarking-noisy-quantum-computation\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-lower-gate-error-rates-matter-both-because-they-allow-larger-uncorrected-nisq-ci--043e58605f51\",\"claim-measured-component-error-rates-under-simultaneous-operation-were-low-enough-to-s--6d6ae35745de\",\"claim-the-largest-random-circuits-combined-53-qubits-1-113-single-qubit-gates-430-two--c8ece98aae87\",\"claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\",\"claim-strong-cavity-qed-coupling-supplies-a-physical-regime-in-which-individual-atoms--9807d4e35625\",\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\",\"claim-controlled-cavity-pulses-can-generate-entanglement-first-between-an-atom-and-an--ee045e1c7175\",\"claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"This topic synthesizes the hardware-facing requirement shared by quantum computing and quantum networking sources: useful scaling depends not only on more qubits, but on preserving coherence while operations, measurements, and interfaces become larger and more complex. In the NISQ and Sycamore sources this pressure appears as two-qubit gate errors, readout errors, circuit depth, and predicted fidelity. In the quantum-internet source it appears as the need for reversible interconnects that convert quantum states between matter and light while preserving coherence and entanglement.\",\"heading\":\"Shared concept\"},{\"body\":\"The NISQ source argues that lower gate error rates matter because they permit larger uncorrected circuits and reduce the future overhead of quantum error correction. The Sycamore source gives a concrete processor-scale example: simultaneous-operation component errors were low enough to support a fidelity model, and the largest random circuits combined 53 qubits, 1,113 single-qubit gates, 430 two-qubit gates, and measurement on each qubit with predicted measurable fidelity. These claims make local processor scaling an error-budget problem as much as a qubit-count problem.\",\"heading\":\"Processor scaling\"},{\"body\":\"The quantum-internet source describes the networking analogue through reversible light-matter interfaces, strong cavity-QED coupling, dark-state mappings, controlled cavity pulses, and EIT-based ensemble memories. These mechanisms aim to move quantum states between stationary atoms or ensembles and flying photons without destroying entanglement. A page on this topic can compare local processor scaling with network scaling: both need error-aware physical mechanisms, but networked systems add conversion between matter and light, heterogeneous nodes, and entanglement-preserving interfaces as first-class design constraints.\",\"heading\":\"Network interfaces\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Coherent interfaces for scaling quantum systems\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-coherent-interfaces-for-scaling-quantum-systems\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-large-scale-quantum-random-access-memory-and-quantum-state-readout-constraints-c--fa6ae1d801a4\",\"claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc\",\"claim-circuit-depth-and-implementation-overhead-can-become-prohibitive-for-nominally-e--07b698d82789\",\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\",\"claim-measured-component-error-rates-under-simultaneous-operation-were-low-enough-to-s--6d6ae35745de\",\"claim-experimental-energy-estimates-are-limited-by-photon-source-impurity-photon-disti--780254eb8ba5\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"The QML source states that loading large classical datasets can require exponential time without qRAM and that reading full solution vectors or principal components can be exponentially hard. These caveats constrain linear-algebra speedups such as HHL and qPCA, especially when the desired answer is classical data rather than a quantum state or compact statistic.\",\"heading\":\"Input and output bottlenecks\"},{\"body\":\"NISQ evidence adds that uncorrected noisy circuits cannot grow far before noise overwhelms the signal, while scalable fault-tolerant computing requires large physical-qubit overhead. Sycamore and VQE sources show useful experiments under these constraints, but also expose fidelity, calibration, and measurement limits.\",\"heading\":\"Hardware noise and fault-tolerance costs\"},{\"body\":\"Across sources, scalability is not determined by asymptotic gate counts alone. Data loading, measurement demands, circuit depth, error rates, and correction overhead jointly decide whether a proposed quantum advantage remains meaningful.\",\"heading\":\"Synthesis claim\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Data access, readout, and error overheads shape whether quantum algorithms scale\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-data-access-readout-and-error-overheads\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268\",\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"claim-the-sycamore-superconducting-processor-created-random-circuit-quantum-states-on--2b4eeabd4063\",\"claim-the-dlcz-protocol-creates-heralded-entanglement-between-atomic-ensembles-by-inte--aa516185d3b2\",\"claim-atomic-ensemble-experiments-had-achieved-stored-heralded-entanglement-high-retri--7d38956d9ede\",\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"This topic treats entanglement as the common resource behind quantum advantage claims, many-body NISQ exploration, random-circuit hardness, and quantum-network protocols, while also noting that entanglement makes control, verification, and scaling difficult. The NISQ source identifies highly entangled quantum dynamics as a natural arena for meaningful quantum advantage and describes noisy devices as experimental tools for exploring many-body quantum physics. The Sycamore source uses random circuits to create hard-to-simulate 53-qubit quantum states. The quantum-internet source shifts the same resource from one processor to distributed nodes and channels.\",\"heading\":\"Shared concept\"},{\"body\":\"In the computing sources, entanglement is tied to both opportunity and constraint. Preskill's claims support the idea that many-body entangled dynamics may yield valuable insight before full fault tolerance. Sycamore's random-circuit experiment supports the idea that unstructured output distributions become exponentially harder to simulate as qubits and cycles grow, and that the processor created states in a 2^53-dimensional state space. These claims justify a concept page about entanglement, but not a blanket claim that every entangled device is practically useful.\",\"heading\":\"Computing evidence\"},{\"body\":\"The quantum-internet claims show entanglement as a distributed resource created, stored, retrieved, and verified across physical systems. The DLCZ protocol creates heralded entanglement between atomic ensembles by interfering emitted single-photon fields and conditioning on a detector event, while experiments had achieved stored heralded entanglement and high retrieval efficiencies. Scalable networks are expected to be heterogeneous systems that require stronger entanglement-verification procedures. The synthesis should therefore frame entanglement as necessary for hard quantum behavior and network connectivity, while emphasizing that practical value depends on fidelity, controllability, memory retrieval, and verification.\",\"heading\":\"Network evidence\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Entanglement as both resource and bottleneck\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-entanglement-as-resource-and-bottleneck\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-device-ansatz-strategies-can-provide-variationally-optimal-solutions-for-the-ava--64cad93bb7ab\",\"claim-unitary-coupled-cluster-ansatz-states-can-be-represented-with-polynomially-many--7f92a3b77387\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-integrated-photonic-processor-prepares-and-measures-arbitrary-t--f41a0c8f645b\",\"claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\",\"claim-strong-cavity-qed-coupling-supplies-a-physical-regime-in-which-individual-atoms--9807d4e35625\",\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\",\"claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\",\"claim-controlled-cavity-pulses-can-generate-entanglement-first-between-an-atom-and-an--ee045e1c7175\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Several sources point toward designing quantum protocols around what a physical platform can reliably prepare, transform, and measure. The photonic variational solver proposes a device ansatz: build the device, characterize the states it can prepare within coherence limits, and optimize within that accessible family. The quantum-internet source treats interfaces similarly at the networking layer, emphasizing reversible conversion between matter and light, cavity-QED interactions, and memory mappings that preserve coherence and entanglement.\",\"heading\":\"Concept\"},{\"body\":\"The shared concept is hardware-native quantum state engineering. Source 04 applies it to computation by using phase shifters, a CNOT gate, photon pairs, and detectors to prepare and measure two-qubit states for energy estimation. Source 03 applies it to communication by using controlled cavity pulses, dark-state adiabatic passage, and electromagnetically induced transparency to map quantum states between stationary matter systems and flying optical fields.\",\"heading\":\"Cross-source synthesis\"},{\"body\":\"This topic is synthesis-worthy because both computation and networking are constrained by physical interfaces, not just abstract algorithms. The evidence supports a page about platform-shaped protocols, while leaving open which hardware-native approaches will scale best.\",\"heading\":\"Implication\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Hardware-Native Interfaces and Ansatz Design\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-hardware-native-interfaces-and-ansatz-design\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\"claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\",\"claim-quantum-expectation-estimation-reduces-coherent-evolution-demands-relative-to-ph--e17864953251\",\"claim-the-quantum-variational-eigensolver-prepares-approximate-ground-states-by-using--0037de1d8464\",\"claim-for-the-demonstrated-4x4-hamiltonian-the-quantum-expectation-estimation-approach--8aea71f20a05\",\"claim-experimental-energy-estimates-are-limited-by-photon-source-impurity-photon-disti--780254eb8ba5\",\"claim-nelder-mead-direct-search-was-more-robust-than-gradient-descent-for-the-noisy-ph--c886fbe39dc2\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Near-term quantum algorithms can be framed as hybrid workflows that keep coherent quantum circuits short while outsourcing parameter search and aggregation to classical computation. The photonic variational eigensolver illustrates this pattern by estimating Hamiltonian expectation values through repeated state preparations and Pauli measurements, then using a classical minimizer to improve the Rayleigh-Ritz quotient. Preskill's NISQ discussion supplies the broader constraint: noisy two-qubit gates and measurements limit the useful size of uncorrected circuits, so VQE-like and QAOA-like approaches are plausible testbeds rather than established routes to broad advantage.\",\"heading\":\"Concept\"},{\"body\":\"The shared concept is not simply that hybrid algorithms exist, but that they are architectural responses to limited coherence. Source 04 emphasizes replacing long phase-estimation-style coherent evolution with many short expectation-value measurements; source 01 explains why that trade matters in NISQ hardware, where roughly one thousand fundamental two-qubit operations may already be too many before noise dominates.\",\"heading\":\"Cross-source synthesis\"},{\"body\":\"The evidence supports hybrid shallow algorithms as experimentally meaningful, but not as proven sources of practical speedup. The NISQ source explicitly leaves unresolved whether VQE or QAOA can outperform mature classical approximation methods, while the photonic experiment reports systematic errors, optimizer sensitivity, and degeneracy-related difficulty at larger bond separations.\",\"heading\":\"Limits and open questions\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Hybrid Shallow Quantum Algorithms Under NISQ Noise\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-hybrid-shallow-quantum-algorithms-under-nisq-noise\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\",\"claim-noise-resilient-circuit-design-can-extend-nisq-computational-reach-but-it-may-tr--aed4bcfeaa39\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\",\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\",\"claim-atomic-ensemble-experiments-had-achieved-stored-heralded-entanglement-high-retri--7d38956d9ede\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"This topic compares demonstrated or plausible near-term quantum capabilities with the longer path to robust, scalable systems. It is supported across all three sources, but the strength of evidence differs by domain: Sycamore reports a concrete task-specific sampling demonstration, while NISQ algorithms and large quantum networks remain more conditional roadmaps. The topic can help distinguish scientific progress from overclaims about general-purpose quantum computing or fully scalable quantum networking.\",\"heading\":\"Shared concept\"},{\"body\":\"The NISQ source distinguishes experimental value and heuristic testbeds from transformative fault-tolerant applications. QAOA and VQE are plausible NISQ-era testbeds, but their ability to outperform mature classical approximation methods remains unresolved. Quantum computers are not expected to efficiently solve hard NP-hard combinatorial optimization instances, and scalable fault-tolerant quantum computing depends on quantum error correction with heavy physical-qubit and gate overhead. Noise-resilient circuit design may extend reach, but may also make circuits easier to simulate classically.\",\"heading\":\"Near-term computing limits\"},{\"body\":\"The Sycamore source reports random-circuit sampling speedup and an elided 53-qubit, 20-cycle fidelity estimate, while explicitly leaving applications such as Shor-style factoring dependent on fault-tolerant logical qubits. The quantum-internet source surveys primitive but real demonstrations of stored heralded entanglement and retrieval efficiency, yet describes robust scalable network protocols, repeaters, local processing, error-corrected teleportation, and scalable verification as ambitious goals. A page on this concept should state that near-term devices can be scientifically important and sometimes classically hard, while the evidence does not support broad claims that they already deliver general-purpose fault-tolerant quantum systems.\",\"heading\":\"Demonstration versus roadmap\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Near-term demonstrations versus fault-tolerant quantum systems\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-near-term-demonstrations-versus-fault-tolerant-systems\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\"claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268\",\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"claim-scalable-fault-tolerant-quantum-computing-depends-on-quantum-error-correction-bu--cf48bc246343\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Preskill characterizes NISQ devices as experimental tools for exploring many-body quantum physics and as stepping stones toward more powerful quantum technologies. This aligns with the Sycamore result as a demonstration of classically hard behavior in a specific sampling task rather than a claim that noisy processors are already broadly useful machines.\",\"heading\":\"Near-term scientific role\"},{\"body\":\"Highly entangled quantum dynamics is presented as the most natural arena for meaningful quantum advantage, and hybrid QAOA or VQE approaches remain plausible NISQ-era testbeds. At the same time, the evidence does not support expecting near-term quantum computers to efficiently solve hard NP-hard optimization instances, and the random-circuit speedup does not by itself establish general application value.\",\"heading\":\"Plausible and uncertain applications\"},{\"body\":\"Both sources separate near-term noisy demonstrations from the longer-term goal of scalable fault-tolerant quantum computing. Preskill emphasizes the heavy physical-qubit overhead of quantum error correction, while the Sycamore source notes that applications such as Shor-style factoring still require fault-tolerant logical qubits.\",\"heading\":\"Fault-tolerant horizon\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Near-Term Quantum Value Versus Fault-Tolerant Promise\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-near-term-value-versus-fault-tolerant-promise\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-nisq-computers-with-roughly-50-to-a-few-hundred-qubits-mark-a-classically-hard-s--2d5ec194bedf\",\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-the-sycamore-superconducting-processor-created-random-circuit-quantum-states-on--2b4eeabd4063\",\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Preskill frames devices with roughly 50 to a few hundred noisy qubits as a threshold where brute-force classical simulation becomes difficult, while noise still sharply limits useful computation. The Sycamore experiment provides a concrete example of that threshold: a 53-qubit superconducting processor created random-circuit quantum states in a 2^53-dimensional state space.\",\"heading\":\"NISQ threshold\"},{\"body\":\"The Sycamore result connects the NISQ regime to random-circuit sampling, where output distributions become exponentially harder to simulate classically as qubit count and circuit depth increase. For the hardest reported sampling task, the authors reported one million samples in about 200 seconds and estimated that equal-fidelity classical sampling would require about 10,000 years on one million cores.\",\"heading\":\"Task-specific speedup\"},{\"body\":\"The speedup is evidence for a narrow random-circuit sampling task, not a general solution to near-term quantum computing limitations. Both sources keep the result within a noise-limited NISQ frame and distinguish it from the broader promise of fault-tolerant quantum algorithms.\",\"heading\":\"Limits of the claim\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"NISQ Scale, Noise, and Random-Circuit Quantum Advantage\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-nisq-scale-and-random-circuit-advantage\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"claim-quantum-principal-component-analysis-can-diagonalize-a-covariance-like-density-m--6ee32a171ac2\",\"claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc\",\"claim-the-near-term-viability-of-quantum-machine-learning-depends-on-solving-input-out--0091df09ad90\",\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Quantum machine learning claims identify speedups for pattern recognition, linear algebra, principal components, and linear-system solving, but the same source stresses that input, output, costing, and benchmarking constraints determine whether those speedups become practical. This aligns with NISQ cautions that mature classical approximation methods remain strong competitors and that quantum computers are not expected to efficiently solve hard NP-hard instances in general.\",\"heading\":\"Why asymptotic speedups are not enough\"},{\"body\":\"Random-circuit sampling on Sycamore provides a concrete task-specific super-classical benchmark, while the QML source frames speedup by lower query or gate complexity under particular access assumptions. Together they support a topic centered on distinguishing demonstrable sampling advantage from broadly useful algorithmic advantage.\",\"heading\":\"Task-specific demonstrations versus reusable advantage\"},{\"body\":\"The available evidence supports a cautious synthesis: advantage is credible for selected tasks and models, but each claimed gain depends on hardware errors, data loading, readout, circuit costs, and comparison against optimized classical methods.\",\"heading\":\"Evidence boundaries\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Practical quantum advantage depends on benchmarks, access models, and classical baselines\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-practical-quantum-advantage-benchmarks-and-bottlenecks\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-nisq-computers-with-roughly-50-to-a-few-hundred-qubits-mark-a-classically-hard-s--2d5ec194bedf\",\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\",\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"claim-linear-cross-entropy-benchmarking-provides-a-fidelity-measure-by-comparing-exper--4abac38b173d\",\"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\",\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"claim-quantum-connectivity-gives-linked-nodes-a-state-space-that-scales-exponentially--50cc8b700a70\",\"claim-full-density-matrix-characterization-becomes-an-impractical-verification-strateg--65a0be3566e1\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"This topic connects NISQ-era expectations, Sycamore random-circuit sampling, and quantum-network verification around a shared problem: quantum systems can enter classically hard state spaces before they become easy to validate or use fault-tolerantly. Preskill frames roughly 50 to a few hundred noisy qubits as a classically hard threshold while emphasizing that gate errors and measurement errors place serious limits on uncorrected circuits. The Sycamore source reports a task-specific random-circuit sampling demonstration in a 53-qubit state space, while the quantum-internet source shows that quantum connectivity expands the state space across linked nodes and makes direct density-matrix characterization impractical as networks grow.\",\"heading\":\"Shared concept\"},{\"body\":\"The Sycamore claims support quantum advantage through random circuits whose output distributions become exponentially harder to simulate classically, linear cross-entropy benchmarking, and agreement among full, patch, elided, and predicted fidelities on verifiable circuits. That evidence is strong for the reported sampling task, including the estimate that one million samples took about 200 seconds on the processor versus a much larger classical cost at equal fidelity. It remains limited because the demonstrated speedup is specific to random circuit sampling and does not remove the need for fault-tolerant logical qubits for broader applications.\",\"heading\":\"Evidence and limits\"},{\"body\":\"The quantum-network source extends the same verification tension from processors to distributed systems. Quantum connectivity gives linked nodes an exponentially larger joint state space, while full density-matrix characterization becomes an impractical verification strategy. A synthesis page should therefore emphasize both the evidential strength of task-specific benchmarks and the unresolved challenge of scalable certification for noisy processors and heterogeneous quantum networks.\",\"heading\":\"Network extension\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Quantum advantage under verification and noise limits\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-quantum-advantage-and-verification-limits\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\",\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"claim-linear-cross-entropy-benchmarking-provides-a-fidelity-measure-by-comparing-exper--4abac38b173d\",\"claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279\",\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"claim-the-photonic-variational-eigensolver-experimentally-recovered-the-he-h-bond-diss--5898494f9b1f\",\"claim-experimental-energy-estimates-are-limited-by-photon-source-impurity-photon-disti--780254eb8ba5\",\"claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Claims of quantum advantage depend on matching a hard-to-simulate quantum process with a verification method that remains credible as classical simulation becomes difficult. The Sycamore random-circuit experiment uses linear cross-entropy benchmarking, elided circuits, and component error models to infer fidelity for circuits whose full output distributions are classically expensive. The photonic variational solver uses expectation-value measurements instead of a supremacy benchmark, but it also relies on quantifying experimental errors and comparing measured outputs with theoretical molecular-energy targets.\",\"heading\":\"Concept\"},{\"body\":\"Source 02 and source 04 share a verification problem: useful quantum experiments must report more than raw device output. Sycamore's evidence links observed bitstrings to ideal probabilities and extrapolates fidelity into harder circuits; the photonic solver links detector counts and Pauli-product estimates to molecular energies while identifying systematic shifts from source, circuit, calibration, coupling, and degeneracy effects.\",\"heading\":\"Cross-source synthesis\"},{\"body\":\"The sources support task-specific experimental milestones rather than general-purpose fault-tolerant computation. Sycamore's speedup is tied to random circuit sampling, while the photonic demonstration is a proof-of-principle molecular-energy calculation on a small Hamiltonian. Both require careful caveats about what the measured task does and does not imply.\",\"heading\":\"Boundary of the evidence\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Quantum Advantage Requires Verifiable Hardness and Error Models\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-quantum-advantage-requires-verifiable-hardness-and-error-models\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-for-quantum-data-can-reduce-tomography-and-characteriza--b02ec76133c0\",\"claim-quantum-principal-component-analysis-can-diagonalize-a-covariance-like-density-m--6ee32a171ac2\",\"claim-full-density-matrix-characterization-becomes-an-impractical-verification-strateg--65a0be3566e1\",\"claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\",\"claim-quantum-connectivity-gives-linked-nodes-a-state-space-that-scales-exponentially--50cc8b700a70\",\"claim-scalable-quantum-networks-are-likely-to-be-heterogeneous-systems-that-combine-ca--dfe53fef0772\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"Quantum machine learning for quantum data can extract principal components, dynamics, or expectation-value summaries with fewer measurements than full state reconstruction. The quantum-internet source independently warns that full density-matrix characterization fails as networks grow because the state description scales exponentially.\",\"heading\":\"Avoiding full tomography\"},{\"body\":\"The photonic VQE source shows that broad Hamiltonian classes can be reduced to measured Pauli-product expectation values, providing another example of replacing full state knowledge with task-relevant summaries. This connects quantum-data learning, molecular energy estimation, and network verification around the common problem of extracting useful evidence from exponentially large state spaces.\",\"heading\":\"Expectation values as compact observables\"},{\"body\":\"The sources do not establish a universal replacement for tomography. They instead support a family of summary-based strategies whose reliability depends on the target observable, access model, and verification protocol.\",\"heading\":\"Verification uncertainty\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"source-03-the-quantum-internet--cd7f6b2f11e2\",\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Quantum data workflows seek useful summaries without full state reconstruction\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-quantum-data-summaries-without-full-state-reconstruction\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-circuit-depth-and-implementation-overhead-can-become-prohibitive-for-nominally-e--07b698d82789\",\"claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc\",\"claim-the-quantum-variational-eigensolver-prepares-approximate-ground-states-by-using--0037de1d8464\",\"claim-quantum-expectation-estimation-reduces-coherent-evolution-demands-relative-to-ph--e17864953251\",\"claim-device-ansatz-strategies-can-provide-variationally-optimal-solutions-for-the-ava--64cad93bb7ab\",\"claim-current-two-qubit-gate-and-measurement-error-rates-imply-that-uncorrected-nisq-c--68f47af68b82\",\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"The photonic variational eigensolver uses repeated expectation-value measurements inside a classical minimization loop, replacing long coherent phase-estimation evolutions with many short measurements. Quantum machine learning has a parallel theme: quantum subroutines can accelerate selected computations, but circuit depth and implementation overhead can erase nominal exponential gains if realistic costs are not controlled.\",\"heading\":\"Hybrid loops reduce coherent runtime demands\"},{\"body\":\"NISQ evidence suggests devices with tens to hundreds of noisy qubits may be valuable experimental tools, but gate errors limit uncorrected circuit depth. Hybrid methods such as VQE and QML routines are therefore synthesis-worthy as approaches that seek useful results before fault tolerance, while remaining vulnerable to noise, optimization difficulty, and classical competition.\",\"heading\":\"NISQ fit and limitations\"},{\"body\":\"Device ansatz strategies in the photonic VQE source show one route to adapting algorithms to available hardware. This complements the QML warning that unoptimized realizations, such as large HHL-style circuits, can become prohibitive despite attractive theoretical scaling.\",\"heading\":\"Hardware-aware ansatz design\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Short-coherence hybrid algorithms adapt quantum computation to noisy devices\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-short-coherence-hybrid-algorithms-for-noisy-devices\"}\n{\"claim_ids\":[\"claim-deep-quantum-learning-can-use-quantum-annealers-programmable-photonic-circuits-a--0bdb973219c3\",\"claim-quantum-boltzmann-machine-training-can-gain-quadratic-improvements-in-thermaliza--2d6a13e72831\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-integrated-photonic-processor-prepares-and-measures-arbitrary-t--f41a0c8f645b\",\"claim-the-photonic-variational-eigensolver-experimentally-recovered-the-he-h-bond-diss--5898494f9b1f\",\"claim-nisq-devices-are-best-understood-as-experimental-tools-for-exploring-many-body-q--fde7f9646dbb\",\"claim-random-quantum-circuits-become-exponentially-harder-to-simulate-classically-as-q--f7cd81f80f31\",\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\"],\"sections\":[{\"body\":\"The QML source allows deep quantum learning to use quantum annealers, programmable photonic circuits, and quantum Boltzmann machines rather than requiring a large universal quantum computer. This connects to the photonic VQE experiment, which demonstrates a task-specific integrated photonic processor, and to NISQ framing that near-term devices are best understood as experimental tools and stepping stones.\",\"heading\":\"Beyond universal fault-tolerant machines\"},{\"body\":\"Quantum Boltzmann machine training claims quadratic improvements in thermalization, sampling, and data access under quantum-coherent or qRAM assumptions. Random-circuit sampling and photonic expectation estimation are different tasks, but they share a broader theme: near-term platforms may be evaluated by how well they produce, sample, or measure quantum distributions under constrained coherence.\",\"heading\":\"Sampling and thermalization as shared primitives\"},{\"body\":\"The evidence supports special-purpose platforms as plausible testbeds, not settled replacements for universal fault-tolerant computation. Their value depends on benchmarked performance against classical methods and on whether hardware-specific advantages survive realistic noise and access assumptions.\",\"heading\":\"Open comparison problem\"}],\"source_ids\":[\"source-05-quantum-machine-learning--a91f0184eb29\",\"source-04-a-variational-eigenvalue-solver-on-a-photonic-quantum-processor--4678297edf5b\",\"source-01-quantum-computing-in-the-nisq-era-and-beyond--2ce59b8ba8bb\",\"source-02-quantum-supremacy-using-a-programmable-superconducting-processor--f98990eb22d8\"],\"structure_type\":\"wiki\",\"title\":\"Special-purpose quantum platforms broaden the near-term learning landscape\",\"topic_id\":\"topic-special-purpose-platforms-for-near-term-quantum-learning\"}\n--- relations compact ---\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"0\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"The dark-state mapping protocol instantiates the general reversible-interconnect requirement.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-9b905f7254c175c67d7f994b7420bf84490519ffa6b20c2a11e25f8ba745c26f\",\"relation_id\":\"derived_from:claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba->claim-large-quantum-networks-require-reversible-interconnects-that-convert-quantum-sta--03b0b3a11218\",\"relation_type\":\"derived_from\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"3\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"4\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"The special promise of quantum dynamics follows from the broader argument that highly entangled systems resist classical simulation.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-3829cfadc2de1fbd047e4c1cb4df2934c3cc391dd753242cd1bd190b631d03d1\",\"relation_id\":\"derived_from:claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268->claim-quantum-computers-have-credible-grounds-for-super-classical-power-because-of-kno--2f85bd581bbb\",\"relation_type\":\"derived_from\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-highly-entangled-quantum-dynamics-is-the-most-natural-arena-for-meaningful-quant--3b6f2f5ba268\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"7\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"1\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"qPCA applies qBLAS-style density-matrix and eigenvalue routines to a specific machine learning task.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-2f0207b35a93ec1a9fbeb853ef559821d216985fb4b950dfdbab6416dd59deed\",\"relation_id\":\"derived_from:claim-quantum-principal-component-analysis-can-diagonalize-a-covariance-like-density-m--6ee32a171ac2->claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"relation_type\":\"derived_from\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-principal-component-analysis-can-diagonalize-a-covariance-like-density-m--6ee32a171ac2\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"2\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"1\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"HHL is one of the linear-algebra primitives that underwrite quantum machine learning speedup claims.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-c98f52f0f751ecaede28701759ec2266df9efdc834d3a31e27b3bba6326ffd35\",\"relation_id\":\"derived_from:claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc->claim-quantum-basic-linear-algebra-subroutines-provide-exponential-speedups-for-fourie--009e83ff60b6\",\"relation_type\":\"derived_from\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-the-hhl-linear-system-algorithm-can-output-a-quantum-state-proportional-to-a-sol--9531ddbd1acc\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"3\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"0\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"QVE uses QEE's Pauli-expectation estimation as the measurement subroutine inside its variational loop.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-ac45217d28a9a77537aea2ce343b998fdec6ebbb596f281107ffab5d0794038d\",\"relation_id\":\"derived_from:claim-the-quantum-variational-eigensolver-prepares-approximate-ground-states-by-using--0037de1d8464->claim-hamiltonian-expectation-values-for-a-broad-class-of-physical-systems-reduce-to-s--ed045d2a43b4\",\"relation_type\":\"derived_from\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-the-quantum-variational-eigensolver-prepares-approximate-ground-states-by-using--0037de1d8464\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"2\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"0\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Large circuit overhead can make asymptotic speedups impractical on realistic machines.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-82cdff2f0589a28fa0d7cd50b83b1028537999ede5a90eef6d84e52c0e18c52d\",\"relation_id\":\"falsifies:claim-circuit-depth-and-implementation-overhead-can-become-prohibitive-for-nominally-e--07b698d82789->claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"relation_type\":\"falsifies\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-circuit-depth-and-implementation-overhead-can-become-prohibitive-for-nominally-e--07b698d82789\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"5\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"0\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Input and output bottlenecks can prevent end-to-end advantage even when an internal quantum subroutine is faster.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-a769f6ad1fd14b243f6411efbb7176032dd5758453503913f713cd50beee1b1f\",\"relation_id\":\"falsifies:claim-large-scale-quantum-random-access-memory-and-quantum-state-readout-constraints-c--fa6ae1d801a4->claim-quantum-machine-learning-can-outperform-classical-algorithms-on-specific-pattern--ade088c638d0\",\"relation_type\":\"falsifies\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-large-scale-quantum-random-access-memory-and-quantum-state-readout-constraints-c--fa6ae1d801a4\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"4\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"3\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Both claims concern reversible mapping between optical fields and matter memories, using different physical platforms.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-0f155a4c952b90287e4b0d71d601e254bec68a9373fef704b216386834737b9c\",\"relation_id\":\"similar:claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba|claim-electromagnetically-induced-transparency-enables-deterministic-reversible-mappin--b76e4e96d4f0\",\"relation_type\":\"similar\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-dark-state-adiabatic-control-can-reversibly-map-a-single-photon-optical-field-in--55c6ef7fe1ba\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"7\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-unitary-coupled-cluster-ansatz-states-can-be-represented-with-polynomially-many--7f92a3b77387\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"9\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Both claims concern ansatz choice as the bridge between available quantum hardware and useful variational states.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-a321265882b8480f710656a8b74a7aca27bef9704e729199118d668e5ee14ca4\",\"relation_id\":\"similar:claim-device-ansatz-strategies-can-provide-variationally-optimal-solutions-for-the-ava--64cad93bb7ab|claim-unitary-coupled-cluster-ansatz-states-can-be-represented-with-polynomially-many--7f92a3b77387\",\"relation_type\":\"similar\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-device-ansatz-strategies-can-provide-variationally-optimal-solutions-for-the-ava--64cad93bb7ab\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"3\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"1\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Both claims delimit the demonstration as a task-specific milestone rather than a general-purpose fault-tolerant quantum computer.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-04809370c2554a7ce66e03f99322178b11278091075f3a31292d80432a35612a\",\"relation_id\":\"similar:claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3|claim-the-demonstrated-speedup-is-specific-to-random-circuit-sampling-and-does-not-rem--47d4f349751e\",\"relation_type\":\"similar\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-for-the-hardest-reported-random-circuit-sampling-task-sycamore-produced-one-mill--07db9778c4a3\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"8\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"6\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Both claims temper optimization expectations by emphasizing hard classical baselines and unresolved quantum advantage.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-93cd412d7857c494ba3e940992fdc77e6b4cb0db92e110a59d8c17a56a0dcbfc\",\"relation_id\":\"similar:claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767|claim-quantum-computers-are-not-expected-to-efficiently-solve-hard-np-hard-combinatori--0d5f718c4d47\",\"relation_type\":\"similar\",\"src_claim_id\":\"claim-hybrid-qaoa-and-vqe-approaches-are-plausible-nisq-era-testbeds-but-their-ability--31ec67369767\",\"src_claim_ref\":\"5\",\"status\":\"open\"}\n{\"below_040_streak\":0,\"contradiction_confidence_band\":\"unknown\",\"dst_claim_id\":\"claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circuits-yielded-f-xeb-2-24-0-21-10-3-over--0a24f12d0686\",\"dst_claim_ref\":\"3\",\"last_evaluated_run_id\":null,\"rationale\":\"Agreement among verification variants supports extending the elided-circuit fidelity estimate into the harder regime.\",\"relation_file_id\":\"rel-6bad9845e7448745b6abc67ad74a2a1b8096a0867991aca32edd6d5e8fb2412b\",\"relation_id\":\"supports:claim-agreement-among-full-patch-elided-and-predicted-fidelities-on-classically-verifi--c34d4d1d9279->claim-the-largest-elided-53-qubit-20-cycle-circ